/*
 * Concept groups for the C++ API reference, rendered as Doxygen's Topics tab.
 *
 * Membership is declared here rather than in the headers so that editorial
 * taxonomy stays out of mochi_core, which other projects also consume. Symbols
 * are named in the published namespace (superdex), because the Doxygen input
 * filter rewrites mochi -> superdex before parsing; see
 * CppDocsConfig.namespace_rewrites.
 *
 * Group order here is display order -- doxyfile_cpp sets SORT_GROUP_NAMES = NO.
 *
 * Only compounds -- @struct and @class -- can be attached to a group from
 * here. Doxygen silently ignores @enum, @typedef, @var and @fn in a file that
 * is not the symbol's declaration site, so enums, aliases, constants and free
 * functions cannot be grouped without @ingroup in the headers themselves. A
 * group whose membership would be entirely non-compound is therefore not
 * declared at all, rather than rendered as an empty page.
 *
 * A symbol that is not listed here simply does not appear under Topics; it
 * remains reachable through Classes, Namespaces, Files and search. Low-value
 * symbols are deliberately omitted to keep the tree scannable.
 */

